---
title: "The AI demo that died on Monday"
description: "Everyone clapped at the agent. Nobody checked the inbox."
date: "2026-07-20"
tags:
  - ai
  - algility
published: true
layout: docs
---

We once ran a flashy AI walkthrough that made a room go quiet in a good way. Cool responses. Clean UI. Felt like the future.

Monday morning the actual lead sat untouched because the handoff still depended on someone noticing a Slack ping. The demo didn't fail. The system around it did.

That's what Algility is for me now. Less theater. More "does the boring path run when I'm not watching." If it needs a hero every time, it's not done.
